#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gaztag: source album metadata from a Gazelle tracker and organize local music.

The tool links an unaltered source directory to the exact tracker torrent by
matching the directory name against the content name of the ".torrent" files in
a watch directory. The matched torrent yields an infohash (and, when present, a
torrent id parsed from the comment field), either of which identifies the exact
release on the tracker. The tracker response is treated as authoritative for
album-level fields (album, year, album artist, label, catalogue number, release
type, edition/version) and for genre and artwork. Per-track fields (title, track
number, disc number, track artist) are read from the existing curated file tags
and are not overwritten.

Operation is two-phase. The "plan" phase resolves metadata and writes a JSON
plan describing every rename, move, tag change, and artwork fetch without
touching the library. The plan may be hand-edited. The "apply" phase executes a
plan. The "run" command performs both with an interactive confirmation.
"""

